  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061(\\frac{1}{3}) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{1/3}+{e}^{-1/3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
